        <mxCell id="n2_pi" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1.5;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;verticalAlign=top;" value="Raspberry Pi 5&lt;br&gt;fixgateway owns CDC" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="300" x="1020" y="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n2_sch" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;b&gt;CONNECTION SCHEDULE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;FROM              PIN   NET        NANO     CABLE&lt;br&gt;J1 ROLL 4-pin      1    +5V        5V       HOK RED&lt;br&gt;J1                 2    0V         GND      HOK BLACK&lt;br&gt;J1                 3    ROLL A     D2       HOK WHITE  + R1&lt;br&gt;J1                 4    ROLL B     D5       HOK GREEN  + R2&lt;br&gt;J2 PITCH 5-pin     1    +5V        5V       Omron BROWN&lt;br&gt;J2                 2    0V         GND      Omron BLUE&lt;br&gt;J2                 3    PITCH A    D6       Omron BLACK + R3&lt;br&gt;J2                 4    PITCH B    D7       Omron WHITE + R4&lt;br&gt;J2                 5    PITCH Z    D8       Omron ORANGE+ R5&lt;br&gt;Airtalk divider    —    AT RX      D4       10k/18k as-built" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="780" x="40" y="620" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n2_notes" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;b&gt;NOTES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. J1 = 4-pin roll cable plug. J2 = 5-pin pitch cable plug.&lt;br&gt;2. Pin numbers are the Cozy harness standard. Mark both plug and socket.&lt;br&gt;3. Flat single-row plugs. Pin 1 at the key / chamfer (left).&lt;br&gt;4. Do not mix HOK BLACK (0V) with Omron BLACK (A).&lt;br&gt;5. Encoder 0V common with MGL Airtalk GND.&lt;br&gt;6. D3 open in flight. USB &#39;test&#39; only with Airtalk off D4.&lt;br&gt;7. Never drive Airtalk. GPIO is 3.3 V only.&lt;br&gt;8. Pull-ups 4.7 kΩ to Nano 3V3 at the Nano end." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="480" x="840" y="620" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
